Quod, sc. contugium. non longo tempore abisse, ‘had surely passed away soon,’ ‘was sure to pass away soon.’ In oratio recta the sentence would be Won longo tempore abit coniugium, st miles zertt. For this rhetorical use of the perfect to express a future action following with certainty upon the occurrence of a given contingency Drager Historische Syntax p. 233 quotes Fam. xii. 6. 2 S7 conseruatus erit, uicimus, Vert. 111. 62. 145, Liu. xxi. 43. 2, in each passage weczmus ;
